# Inputs to the policy tier of the bundled rule set
#
# The mainland-China set (app/src/main/assets/rules/policy/mainland-china.list)
# is generated from these, by generate-mainland-china.py, and from nothing else.
# Each input is pinned by an immutable address and a checksum, so the asset can
# be regenerated byte for byte and a reviewer can check that it was.
#
# Why these two (D-18, settled 2026-10-24 by the requester):
#
#   * APNIC's delegation statistics are the registry's own record of which
#     address blocks were allocated to holders in CN. Free to use on the
#     condition that APNIC is not held responsible; no attribution is required,
#     and it is given in the asset header anyway. The file records where a
#     block was first allocated, not where it is used today, which is the
#     error such lists always carry and is said so in the asset.
#   * felixonmars/dnsmasq-china-list, accelerated-domains.china.conf: the
#     domains whose authoritative servers are in mainland China, the list most
#     China-direct rule sets are derived from. WTFPL-2.0, which is compatible
#     with GPL-3.0 and asks for nothing. Its apple and google files are not
#     used: they say which CDN a service is reached through, which is a
#     different question from where a name is served.
#
# Cadence: both move daily upstream; this file moves when someone regenerates
# the asset, which should be at least once per release.

APNIC_URL=https://ftp.apnic.net/stats/apnic/2026/delegated-apnic-20261023.gz
APNIC_SHA256=b01b47578ca50e24a667e445f814a8cdb0a0c1bf1cf694f86260451cb992babe
APNIC_LICENCE=APNIC conditions of use (free use, no warranty)

CHINA_LIST_REPO=https://github.com/felixonmars/dnsmasq-china-list
CHINA_LIST_COMMIT=eb9dc5e02c20f9dbcb81e2f868c6cbfc5fc1727f
CHINA_LIST_FILE=accelerated-domains.china.conf
